  "description": "WIDKUS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C176 H222 Co6 Dy6 N6 O52,2(C2 H3 N1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3A (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.265-3.967 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.42-112.02°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C180H232Co6Dy6N8O54. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II), I(II).",
